content.text:
The forwarding setup is in **`modules/home-manager/programs/ssh.nix`**:

```nix
programs.ssh = {
  enable = true;
  enableDefaultConfig = false;

  settings = {
    nixos-desktop = {
      HostName = "10.69.69.183";
      User = "michael";
      ForwardAgent = true;
    };

    "*" = {
      IdentityAgent =
        if isDarwin then
          "\"~/Library/Group Containers/2BUA8C4S2C.com.1password/t/agent.sock\""
        else
          "~/.1password/agent.sock";
    };

    forwarded-agent = lib.hm.dag.entryBefore [ "*" ] {
      header =
        if isDarwin then
          ''Match exec "test ! -S \"%d/Library/.../agent.sock\""''
        else
          ''Match exec "test ! -S \"%d/.1password/agent.sock\""'';
      IdentityAgent = "SSH_AUTH_SOCK";
    };
  };
};
```

In practical terms, Home Manager generates `~/.ssh/config` like:

```sshconfig
Host nixos-desktop
  HostName 10.69.69.183
  User michael
  ForwardAgent yes

# Prefer the local 1Password agent
Host *
  IdentityAgent ~/.1password/agent.sock
```

And the 1Password agent is configured by **`modules/home-manager/files/1password-agent.toml`**:

```toml
[[ssh-keys]]
vault = "Personal"

[[ssh-keys]]
vault = "Infra"
```

So the chain is:

```text
1Password agent → ssh nixos-desktop (ForwardAgent yes)
               → temporary SSH_AUTH_SOCK on nixos-desktop
               → git / ssh can use your forwarded keys
```

The `ForwardAgent = true` line is the specific setting that enables forwarding.

